.TH ENV 1
.SH NAME
env \- print environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Env
prints the process's environment, one variable per line, as
.IR name = value .
The names come from
.BR /env ,
a directory of one file per variable (see
.IR env (3)),
and a value with several elements is printed with a space between
each, in place of the NUL
.IR rc (1)
separates them with in the file.
There are no arguments and no options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
env | grep ^path=
.EE
.SH FILES
.B /env
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/env/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rc (1),
.IR env (3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B "can't open"
if
.B /env
could not be opened.
.SH BUGS
A value of several elements and a value of one element that happens to
contain a space print alike, so
.I env's
output cannot always be told apart from the file it came from.
